            "review_text": "Daydream24323760108\n6 contributions\n0\nA night at Arul House – a place of cuisine not only to eat, but to feel\nJul 2026 • Business\nI came to Arul House with the mind of a man looking for a good meal. But when we leave, what remains is not just the taste, but the feeling of just entering a very different space in the heart of the drug trafficking.\nThe first thing that impressed me was space. Arul House does not try to be luxurious in a fancy style, but chooses warmth and closeness. The wood materials, the gentle golden lights, the indigenous details and the breath of Western culture are present enough to create a relaxing feeling. Sitting here, people are easier to slow down, easier to talk and easier to connect with each other.\nWhat I love more than human beings. From the moment I entered to the moment I left, I felt the sincerity of the service team. Not too stylish, no machines, but gentle and delicate care. It feels like Arul House not only trains the desk staff, but builds people who know how to welcome guests like a familiar.\nAnd then to the culinary culture – the soul part of Arul House. Each dish is not only concerned about the taste but also carries the story of the country. Here, cuisine is not separated from culture. One can feel the spirit of the forest, of the Eden community, of the indigenous materials raised and presented with respect for the homeland.\nRead more\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten July 31, 2026",
